# Unreal Engine generated folders - never version these
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
Build/

# Visual Studio workspace files - regenerated via right-click .uproject > Generate project files
.vs/
*.sln
*.slnx
.vsconfig

# Content is excluded for now: the Content folder holds multi-GB Fab/Megascans packs that
# don't belong in a plain git repo. When project-authored assets (Blueprints, maps, data assets)
# start accumulating, set up Git LFS and start tracking Content/ selectively - the Fab packs
# themselves are always re-downloadable from the Fab library.
Content/

# Plugin build artifacts
Plugins/**/Binaries/
Plugins/**/Intermediate/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-07-26: project-authored Content is now tracked via Git LFS.
# Fab/Megascans packs stay excluded - they are re-downloadable from the Fab
# library and would bloat the repo (DreamscapeSeries alone is 2.2 GB).
# Content/ is still ignored by default above; these negations opt specific
# project-authored folders back in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!Content/
Content/*
!Content/Characters/
!Content/Blueprints/
!Content/UI/
!Content/Input/
!Content/Maps/
!Content/VFX/
# 2026-08-04: BB_Human / BT_Militia / DA_Race_Human live here. Without this negation the entire
# defender AI layer was untracked and would have been lost on any clean checkout.
!Content/AI/

# 2026-08-05: the same class of bug as Content/AI above, found while pushing the ranged-combat
# work. Both of these are project-authored and neither was versioned.
#
#   Content/Python/  the editor authoring scripts (gs_build_burn_material.py builds the whole burn
#                    material stack; gs_build_aim_materials.py builds the aim arc + reticle). Plain
#                    text, no LFS. These GENERATE assets, so losing them means losing the ability to
#                    rebuild or retune what they made - strictly worse than losing an asset.
#   Content/Data/    DA_Weapon_Scout and friends. Weapon identity is a data operation in this
#                    project (design doc §5), so this folder is gameplay design, not imported art.
!Content/Python/
!Content/Data/

# 2026-08-27 (#329/#330): the SAME class of bug a FOURTH time. Content/EditorTools/ holds
# EUW_GSRoadTools and EUW_GSMarkerTools - the road-drawing and marker-tagging panels. They are
# authored tooling (each button is a wired ExecutePythonCommand graph), they took a session to
# build, and they were sitting untracked. Same reasoning as Content/Python above: losing the tool
# is worse than losing an asset, because the tool is what rebuilds the asset.
!Content/EditorTools/

# 2026-08-21 (#249): the SAME class of bug a third time. Content/Audio/ held the
# three hand-authored horn SoundWaves - the only project-authored audio in the
# project - and was untracked, so a clean checkout lost them silently. It now
# also holds the whole mixer spine (sound classes, submixes, attenuation,
# concurrency, the base mix and the surface physical materials), which is
# authored configuration, not imported art. None of it is re-downloadable.
!Content/Audio/

# 2026-08-24 (#270): a FOURTH instance of the same bug. Content/Items/ holds the ACF item and
# weapon Blueprints - BP_Item_GoblinAxe and BP_ACFWeapon_GoblinAxe. These are not imported art;
# they are the data half of the ACF equipment migration, and DA_Char_HordeGoblin (already tracked,
# under the Content/Data negation above) points straight at BP_Item_GoblinAxe. Without this line a
# clean checkout gets a character data asset referencing an item class that is not in the repo,
# which fails as a goblin that silently spawns unarmed - the exact symptom #270 spent a session
# chasing for a different reason.
!Content/Items/

# 2026-09-09 (#406): Content/FullSample/ is DELIBERATELY NOT NEGATED. Read this before
# "fixing" it to match the lines above.
#
# It is the official Ascent Combat Framework Ultimate sample content (~4.7 GB), copied in
# from D:\ACFUSampleProject4.2\FullSample so the 40 ACF skill packs stop citing /Game/FullSample/
# paths that have never resolved on this machine. It is marketplace content, it is not ours,
# and it is re-downloadable from the ACF repo - the same reasoning as Plugins/Marketplace/
# below, and the exact opposite of the six negations above, every one of which exists because
# project-authored work was silently untracked.
#
# The default Content/ ignore already covers it. This comment exists only so the next reader
# recognises it as a decision rather than the seventh instance of that bug.
#
# AMENDED 2026-09-10 (#416): the BULK of FullSample stays ignored, but the exact dependency
# closure of the animation stack our characters run is now TRACKED, below.
#
# Why: `BP_ErikaArcher` runs ACF's own `ACF_Humanoid_ABP` directly - no conform script, no
# retarget library, no duplicated assets, which is the whole point of the ACF conversion. That
# makes a shipping character depend on gitignored content: a package built on this machine is
# fine, but a clean `git clone` opens with a broken archer and no obvious reason why.
#
# The closure was MEASURED, not guessed: walking hard dependencies from `ACF_Humanoid_ABP`
# reaches **292 packages totalling 126.4 MB** - 2.7% of FullSample. Dominated by
# `Animations/Locomotion` (201: the Unarmed, Rifle and Pistol movesets) and `AimOffsets` (48).
#
# Negating the closure IN PLACE is deliberately preferred over copying those assets into
# `Content/Characters/`: duplication would mean repointing every reference and would permanently
# FORK them from ACF, so plugin updates would silently stop reaching our characters. Tracked in
# place, they still update when FullSample is re-copied.
#
# If a future character needs something outside these folders, re-measure the closure rather than
# adding paths by guesswork - the measurement script is in ticket #416.
!Content/FullSample/
Content/FullSample/*
!Content/FullSample/Animations/
Content/FullSample/Animations/*
!Content/FullSample/Animations/ACF_Humanoid_ABP.uasset
!Content/FullSample/Animations/BS_MM_Rifle_Jog_Leans.uasset
!Content/FullSample/Animations/Locomotion/
!Content/FullSample/Animations/AimOffsets/
!Content/FullSample/Animations/OriginalAnimations/
!Content/FullSample/Animations/AnimBPs/
!Content/FullSample/Animations/Rider/
!Content/FullSample/Animations/ForwardFacing/
# GASP is negated FILE BY FILE, deliberately. Negating the two directories the closure touches
# (`GASP/Animations/`, `GASP/UEFN_Mannequin/`) tracked **1,056 files / 1,049 MB** - the whole
# Game Animation Sample motion-matching database - where the closure needs exactly SEVEN packages.
# Caught by measuring the staged size before committing, not after. Directory negation tracks the
# DIRECTORY; it does not track "the files in it that something references".
!Content/FullSample/GASP/
Content/FullSample/GASP/*
!Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/
Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/*
!Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/Overlays/
Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/Overlays/*
!Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/Overlays/ACF_MMBaseOverlay.uasset
!Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/Overlays/ACF_MMBowOverlay.uasset
!Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/Overlays/ACF_MMSwordOverlay.uasset
!Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/Overlays/Poses/
Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/Overlays/Poses/*
!Content/FullSample/GASP/Animations/Overlays/Poses/Protector_Idle1.uasset
!Content/FullSample/GASP/UEFN_Mannequin/
Content/FullSample/GASP/UEFN_Mannequin/*
!Content/FullSample/GASP/UEFN_Mannequin/Meshes/
Content/FullSample/GASP/UEFN_Mannequin/Meshes/*
!Content/FullSample/GASP/UEFN_Mannequin/Meshes/SKM_UEFN_Mannequin.uasset
!Content/FullSample/GASP/UEFN_Mannequin/Meshes/SKM_UEFN_Mannequin_Physics.uasset
!Content/FullSample/GASP/UEFN_Mannequin/Meshes/SK_UEFN_Mannequin.uasset
# The bow PROP is outside the AnimBP's dependency closure - it is a weapon item, referenced by the
# weapon Blueprint rather than by the animation graph - so the measured closure above does not
# reach it. Added explicitly (1.6 MB): the mesh, its own `Bow_Skeleton`, `Bow_AnimBP` and the
# draw/loop/release montages that animate the STRING, plus the arrow and the bow audio cues.
# `UACFBowAnimInstance` drives the string from a socket named `Arrow` (`ACFBowAnimInstance.cpp:17`).
!Content/FullSample/Assets/
Content/FullSample/Assets/*
!Content/FullSample/Assets/Weapons/
Content/FullSample/Assets/Weapons/*
!Content/FullSample/Assets/Weapons/Bow/
!Content/FullSample/Assets/Items/
Content/FullSample/Assets/Items/*
!Content/FullSample/Assets/Items/BowAndArrow/
!Content/FullSample/Audio/
Content/FullSample/Audio/*
!Content/FullSample/Audio/Bow/

# source FBX staging lives outside Content (auto-import fires on anything
# under Content/) and is not versioned - the clips come from Mixamo.
_MixamoStaging/

# Fab plugin copied into the project - reinstallable from Fab
Plugins/Marketplace/

# 2026-08-13 (#150): ACF's 40 author-written Claude skill packs are copied out of the
# plugin into .claude/skills by Tools/Register-ACFSkills.ps1. That directory USED to be
# ignored here as regenerable marketplace content.
#
# UN-IGNORED 2026-08-28 (#340/#341, Michael's call). It is no longer only marketplace
# content. The #340 workflow wrote 9 project-specific `gs-*` packs that nothing can
# regenerate, and project findings have since been written INTO the ACF-derived packs -
# e.g. the every-other-waypoint claim in gs-ai-patrol-advancers and ai-framework was
# refuted in PIE and corrected by hand. Ignoring the directory meant hours of mining and
# hard-won corrections sat one Register-ACFSkills.ps1 run from deletion, unversioned.
#
# CONSEQUENCE: re-running Register-ACFSkills.ps1 after an ACF update will overwrite the
# ACF-derived packs and clobber any hand corrections in them. That now shows up as a git
# diff instead of vanishing silently - read the diff before committing it.

# Local secrets - never commit (Anthropic API key for the content pipeline)
.env
.env.*
